# One round of tcc compiling itself.
#
# tcc is built by the round below it and links against that round's library
# (-B), and each round is allowed more of C than the last: long long, then
# bitfields, then floats.  The first round was compiled by MesCC and knows
# almost none of it; by the last, tcc compiles itself with what a normal
# build would use.  The flags are upstream's, from the fork's own boot.sh.
#
# Every option is its own variable because kaem substitutes a variable as a
# SINGLE argument: a variable holding "-D A=1 -D B=1" arrives as one option
# that tcc cannot read.  kaem cannot loop either, so the slots are fixed and
# a round fills what it needs; an unused slot repeats a harmless flag rather
# than being empty, which kaem would pass as an empty argument.
#
# config.h is empty -- catm with no inputs makes it so -- because everything
# it would say is passed as -D here.
#
# The \" are kaem's escape for a literal quote, and they are not decoration:
# these defines are STRING literals in C, and kaem strips an ordinary quote
# while grouping.  Without the escape tcc is handed TCC_LIBGCC=libc.a, which
# expands to a bare identifier and fails to compile as `'libc' undeclared`.

cd ${TMPDIR}
${bin_catm} config.h
${bin_mkdir} -p ${out}/bin

${prevTcc} -B ${prevLibs}/lib -g -v -o ${out}/bin/tcc -D BOOTSTRAP=1 ${opt1} ${opt2} ${opt3} ${opt4} ${opt5} ${opt6} ${opt7} ${opt8} ${opt9} ${opt10} -I . -I ${src} -D TCC_TARGET_${tccTarget}=1 -D CONFIG_TCCDIR=\"\" -D CONFIG_SYSROOT=\"\" -D CONFIG_TCC_CRTPREFIX=\"{B}\" -D CONFIG_TCC_ELFINTERP=\"\" -D CONFIG_TCC_LIBPATHS=\"{B}\" -D CONFIG_TCC_SYSINCLUDEPATHS=${sysIncludePaths} -D TCC_LIBGCC=\"libc.a\" -D TCC_LIBTCC1=\"libtcc1.a\" -D CONFIG_TCCBOOT=1 -D CONFIG_TCC_STATIC=1 -D CONFIG_USE_LIBGCC=1 -D TCC_MES_LIBC=1 -D TCC_VERSION=\"0.9.28-${version}\" -D ONE_SOURCE=1 ${src}/tcc.c
